Appearance: Brahma Kamal is an exquisite flower with large, white petals arranged in layers, resembling a lotus in appearance. It blooms only during the night and emits a sweet fragrance.

Habitat: This flower is found in the alpine regions of the Himalayas, typically at altitudes ranging from 3,000 to 4,600 meters (9,800 to 15,100 feet). It thrives in cool, moist environments with well-drained soil.

Cultural Significance: Brahma Kamal holds significant cultural and religious importance in Hindu mythology and Tibetan Buddhism. It is considered sacred and is often associated with various deities and spiritual practices.

Mythological Connections: According to Hindu mythology, Brahma Kamal is believed to be the favorite flower of Lord Brahma, the creator of the universe. It is also associated with other Hindu deities such as Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati.

Rare and Endangered: Due to its limited habitat and environmental threats, Brahma Kamal is considered rare and endangered. Its conservation is a matter of concern for environmentalists and conservationists.', NULL, NULL, '2026-08-17T15:47:40.040Z', '2026-08-20T11:38:39.535Z', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Brahma Kamal, also known as Saussurea obvallata or the King of Himalayan Flowers, is a rare and revered flower native to the Himalayan region. Here are some k', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Bramha Kamal');
