Appearance: Hoya Variegated features glossy, waxy leaves with variegation, which can include patches, stripes, or speckles of different colors such as white, cream, or yellow. The variegation adds visual interest to the plant and enhances its ornamental value.

Cultivation: Hoya Variegated is typically grown as a houseplant, although it can also be cultivated outdoors in warm climates. It thrives in bright, indirect light and well-draining soil. Allow the soil to dry out slightly between waterings, as Hoyas are susceptible to root rot if overwatered.

Maintenance: Hoya Variegated is relatively low-maintenance and requires minimal care once established. Prune the plant occasionally to maintain its shape and remove any dead or damaged foliage. Regular fertilization during the growing season can promote healthy growth and vibrant foliage.

Flowering: Like other Hoyas, Variegated Hoya can produce clusters of small, star-shaped flowers. The flowers are often fragrant and can range in color from white to pink to red, depending on the specific cultivar.

Propagation: Hoya Variegated can be propagated through stem cuttings. Simply cut a section of stem with a few nodes and place it in well-draining potting mix. Keep the soil moist until roots develop, and then transplant the cutting into its own container.', NULL, NULL, '2026-08-17T15:47:40.040Z', '2026-08-20T11:38:39.535Z', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Hoya Variegated, also known as Variegated Hoya, is a cultivar of the Hoya genus, prized for its attractive variegated foliage. Here are some key details about', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Hoya Verigated');
