Maintenance: Peperomias are relatively low-maintenance plants. They do not require frequent repotting and are not heavy feeders. Prune the plants occasionally to remove dead or yellowing leaves and promote bushier growth.

Propagation: Peperomias can be easily propagated from stem cuttings or leaf cuttings. Simply cut a section of stem or leaf with a node and place it in well-draining soil or water until roots develop. Once rooted, the cuttings can be potted up into their own containers.

Versatility: Peperomias are versatile and can be used in various ways in indoor settings. They are well-suited for terrariums, mixed planters, and hanging baskets, or they can be displayed individually in pots or containers.', NULL, NULL, '2026-08-17T15:47:40.040Z', '2026-08-20T11:38:39.535Z', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Peperomia plants are a diverse and popular group of small houseplants appreciated for their ornamental foliage and ease of care. Here are some key details abo', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Peperomia Plant');
