Appearance: The Pink Princess Philodendron features heart-shaped leaves with vibrant pink variegation that contrasts beautifully with the deep green color of the foliage. The pink variegation can vary in intensity, with some leaves displaying more pink than others.

Cultivation: Pink Princess Philodendrons are typically grown as indoor houseplants. They prefer bright, indirect light but can also tolerate lower light conditions. Allow the soil to dry out partially between waterings, as overwatering can lead to root rot. Provide support such as a moss pole or trellis for the plant to climb.

Maintenance: Pink Princess Philodendrons require regular maintenance to maintain their vibrant foliage. Prune the plant occasionally to remove any all-green leaves that may appear, as these can detract from the overall appearance of the plant. Regularly wipe the leaves with a damp cloth to remove dust and keep them looking their best.

Propagation: Pink Princess Philodendrons can be propagated from stem cuttings. Simply cut a section of stem with a node and place it in water or moist soil until roots develop. Once rooted, the cutting can be potted up into its own container.

Versatility: Pink Princess Philodendrons are versatile and can be used in various ways in indoor settings. They can be grown in hanging baskets, on shelves, or as trailing plants in containers. Their unique foliage adds a pop of color and interest to any space.', NULL, NULL, '2026-08-17T15:47:40.040Z', '2026-08-20T11:38:39.535Z', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The Pink Princess is a cultivar of the Philodendron genus, known for its stunning pink variegation on its leaves. Here are some key details about the Pink Pri', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Pink Princess');
